'''archæonomous''' (är-kē-on′ọ̄-mus), ''a.'' [< Gr. ἀρχαιόνομος, old-fashioned, < ἀρχαῖος, ancient, old, + νόμος, law, custom.] Retaining, or deviating little from, a primitive condition; old-fashioned: especially applied by S. Loven to echinoids of the family ''Clypeastridæ''. [Rare.]

